WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.432
How do edge chemistry and dispersion corrections change electronic predictions?

2
00:00:05.118 --> 00:00:10.057
My capstone investigates pentagonal palladium diselenide nanoribbons through density functional

3
00:00:10.057 --> 00:00:11.530
theory calculations.

4
00:00:13.083 --> 00:00:18.666
I modelled four hydrogen-passivated edge families: A A, Z Z, Z A, and S S.

5
00:00:18.666 --> 00:00:24.362
Fluorine and hydroxyl substitutions at central and lateral sites created four modified configurations.

6
00:00:25.917 --> 00:00:31.354
Using Materials Studio and CASTEP, I optimised atomic structures and inspected band structures

7
00:00:31.354 --> 00:00:32.790
and density of states.

8
00:00:33.476 --> 00:00:38.055
The pristine comparison covers P B E, Grimme, and the T S correction.

9
00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:45.175
For the pristine A A three example, the reported band gap is zero point five eight seven electronvolts

10
00:00:45.175 --> 00:00:48.796
with P B E, and zero point five eight one with Grimme.

11
00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:55.593
Across the four modified structures, Grimme gaps range from zero point eight seven zero to zero

12
00:00:55.593 --> 00:00:57.891
point nine zero seven electronvolts.

13
00:00:58.577 --> 00:01:03.071
The corresponding P B E predictions are lower, as the thesis table shows.

14
00:01:04.617 --> 00:01:08.541
These reported calculations demonstrate sensitivity to the chosen method.

15
00:01:09.227 --> 00:01:11.853
They do not establish experimental accuracy.

16
00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:17.904
Explore the original models, plots, calculation settings, and limitations in the full project

17
00:01:17.904 --> 00:01:18.600
page.
